From: JiaY-shi <shi05275@163.com>
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath12k: keep four-address peers on the mac80211 path

Native Direct Switch attaches an authorized peer to its AP netdev. A WDS
peer is subsequently moved into a per-station AP/VLAN by hostapd, but its
PPE RX still enters the ordinary AP. Bridged source addresses are learned
on the wrong port and replies fail to reach the backhaul station.

Withdraw Direct Switch before programming four-address firmware mode; the
routing command can otherwise replace the peer RX settings. Exclude such
peers if authorization happens later. Reject hardware flow paths for them
as well. Ordinary clients can continue using Direct Switch.

Signed-off-by: JiaY-shi <shi05275@163.com>
---
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/mac.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/mac.c
@@ -6740,6 +6740,19 @@
 		arvif = arsta->arvif;
 		ahvif = arvif->ahvif;
 		ar = arvif->ar;
+		dp = ath12k_ab_to_dp(ar->ab);
+		/* Direct Switch binds RX to the AP netdev, not the per-STA
+		 * AP/VLAN. Withdraw an already authorized peer before using
+		 * four-address forwarding through mac80211.
+		 */
+		if (dp->ops->ds_sta_state) {
+			ret = dp->ops->ds_sta_state(ar, arvif, arsta, false);
+			if (ret) {
+				ath12k_warn(ar->ab, "failed to disable Direct Switch for 4addr peer %pM: %d\n",
+					    arsta->addr, ret);
+				return ret;
+			}
+		}
 
 		if (arvif->set_wds_vdev_param)
 			goto skip_nawds;
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/wifi7/ppe_ds.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/wifi7/ppe_ds.c
@@ -770,6 +770,11 @@
 
 	if (arvif->ahvif->vif->type != NL80211_IFTYPE_AP)
 		return 0;
+	/* Authorization can follow AP/VLAN assignment. Never re-enable
+	 * AP-bound hardware forwarding for a four-address peer.
+	 */
+	if (ahsta->enable_4addr)
+		enable = false;
 	link = ahsta->primary_link_id;
 	if (link >= IEEE80211_MLD_MAX_NUM_LINKS || !(links & BIT(link)))
 		return 0;
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/wifi7/hw.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/wifi7/hw.c
@@ -1175,7 +1175,9 @@
 				   struct net_device_path_ctx *ctx,
 				   struct net_device_path *path)
 {
-	if (vif->type != NL80211_IFTYPE_AP)
+	struct ath12k_sta *ahsta = sta ? ath12k_sta_to_ahsta(sta) : NULL;
+
+	if (vif->type != NL80211_IFTYPE_AP || (ahsta && ahsta->enable_4addr))
 		return -EOPNOTSUPP;
 
 	path->type = DEV_PATH_ETHERNET;
